.Dd February 7, 2009
.Dt pam_launchd 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm pam_launchd
.Nd launchd PAM module
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Op Ar service-name
.Ar function-class
.Ar control-flag
pam_launchd
.Op Ar options
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The launchd PAM module supports the session management function class.  In terms of the
.Ar function-class
parameter, this is the
.Dq Li session
class.
.Pp
The launchd session module is used to move the authenticated session to the correct, per-user, launchd namespace.
.Pp
The following option may be passed to this session management module:
.Bl -tag
.It Cm launchd_session_type=SESSION_TYPE
Move this session to the launchd session type specified.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag
.It Ev launchd_session_type=SESSION_TYPE
Move this session to the launchd session type specified.
.El
.\" NextBSD: the section below documents the NextBSD changes (VENDORED.md).
.Sh NEXTBSD
The module only acts when run as root.
Before it moves the session, it checks the user's per-user
.Xr launchd 8
with two requests, each of which must be answered within 3 seconds.
The first is answered by the per-user launchd itself.
The second looks up
.Li com.apple.system.notification_center ,
a service only PID 1 has, so the per-user launchd must forward it to PID 1.
Any failure, including a missing or unresponsive per-user launchd or one
that does not forward, leaves the session on the root bootstrap and returns
.Dv PAM_IGNORE ,
so a broken per-user launchd never blocks a login.
.Pp
The default session type is
.Li Background :
the session joins the per-user launchd's own
.Li Background
session, which that launchd creates when it starts, and no new session is
created.
.Cm launchd_session_type=StandardIO
is opt-in.
With it, the per-user launchd creates a
.Li StandardIO
session for the login process, runs
.Ic launchctl bootstrap -S StandardIO
in it, which loads the LaunchAgents from all domains
.Pq Ic load -S StandardIO -D all ,
and tears the session down when the login process exits.
On NextBSD the login process is identified to launchd by a port it holds
for its lifetime rather than by its task-name port, so the session also
ends if that process calls
.Xr execve 2 .
If the switch fails, the session stays on the root bootstrap and the
module returns
.Dv PAM_IGNORE .
.Pp
A LaunchAgent loads into a
.Li StandardIO
or
.Li Background
session only if its property list sets
.Li LimitLoadToSessionType
to that session type (a string, or an array that contains it).
.Xr launchctl 1
gives an agent without the key the default
.Li Aqua ,
as on Darwin, and so skips it in every other session.
.Pp
No
.Pa /etc/pam.d
policy file uses this module yet.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Pa /usr/lib/pam_launchd.so.6
the module
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr launchctl 1 ,
.Xr pam.conf 5 ,
.Xr launchd 8 ,
.Xr pam 8
